  "notes": "{生|は}やす is a godan verb meaning to grow (hair, beard, etc.) deliberately.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{生|は}える→生える：02392_haeru⟧ (intransitive: to grow naturally)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦ひげ→ひげ：01332_hige⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{生|は}やす: to grow a beard\n- ⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{生|は}やす: to grow one's hair out\n- ⟦{爪|つめ}→爪：02159_tsume⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{生|は}やす: to let one's nails grow long\n- ⟦{根|ね}→根：03525_ne⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{生|は}やす: to put down roots (also figurative)\n\nUSAGE:\nImplies intentional or deliberate growth, unlike ⟦{生|は}える→生える：02392_haeru⟧ which describes natural, spontaneous growth. {生|は}やす suggests agency—the person chooses to let something grow.",
